  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The small rounded leaves are cupped at the attachment to the leaf- The basal lobes overlap and, with the upturn of the leaf, form a shallow cup. The red leafstalks are sturdy. Leaf color is dark green, becoming bright blends of reds and yellows in the fall. The growth seems less vigorous than that of the species, but the plant forms a small tree to 20 ft. (6 m) tall. It appears to be a sturdy and hardy form. The name means \"small-leaved.\""
  },
